  "created": "2026-10-21T18:29:09.65Z",
  "description": "Version: 0.0.10\n\n\t\t\tAdded:\n\t\t\t- Ambient log context via new INDLogContextAccessor / NDLogContextAccessor\n\t\t\t(AsyncLocal-backed). ServiceName, CorrelationId, and custom unique/filter\n\t\t\tIDs can now be set once at the start of a request or message handler and\n\t\t\tare automatically attached to every subsequent log call within that\n\t\t\tasync flow, without needing to be passed explicitly each time.\n\t\t\t- New overloads on INDLoggerService (LogDebug/LogInformation/LogWarning/\n\t\t\tLogError/LogFatal) that omit serviceName and correlationId, resolving\n\t\t\tthem from ambient context instead. Existing method signatures are\n\t\t\tunchanged and continue to work exactly as before.\n\t\t\t- Explicit-over-ambient precedence: any explicitly passed serviceName,\n\t\t\tcorrelationId, or customUniqueIds value on a log call overrides its\n\t\t\tambient counterpart on a per-key basis; ambient values only fill in\n\t\t\tgaps left by explicit arguments. logs will be give high priority to context values than passed values.\n\n\t\t\tChanged:\n\t\t\t- NDLoggerService now takes a required INDLogContextAccessor dependency\n\t\t\t(registered automatically via AddNDLogging). Consumers using the\n\t\t\tstandard DI extension methods require no changes; only direct\n\t\t\t`new NDLoggerService(...)` call sites need updating.\n\n\t\t\tNotes:\n\t\t\t- No breaking changes to the public INDLoggerService contract for\n\t\t\texisting 7-argument Log* methods.",
  "id": "ND.FW.Observability",
